CAPS7 = {
"73_app_rest_timer": ("B2C","Nobody times their rest properly. The plan does it for you.\n\nThree minutes on a heavy squat. Sixty seconds on calf raises. The difference matters and most people split it down the middle at 90 seconds for everything.\n\nTimer's on every exercise, already set to what that exercise actually needs 🕐","general"),
"74_app_reasoning": ("B2C","Tap any exercise and it tells you why it's in YOUR plan.\n\nNot a generic description of a face pull. The actual reason it's there given what you told us, in this case, nine hours a day at a desk.\n\nDoing the work is easier when you understand the work 🧠","product"),
"75_app_logging": ("B2C","Log what you lifted, right where the plan already is.\n\nNot a second app you'll stop opening by Thursday. Tick it off as you go, and week three shows you exactly what week one looked like.\n\nTwo minutes a session. It's the only honest way to know it's working.","general"),
"76_app_today_view": ("B2C","It opens on today. Not a contents page.\n\nNo scrolling through weeks you already did. No hunting for the right day. Save it to your home screen and it's just there, like any other app.","product"),
"77_app_five_tabs": ("B2C","Five tabs, and you only get the ones you need.\n\nTrain, Morning, Fuel, Recover, plus your details. No nutrition in your plan? The Fuel tab simply isn't there.\n\nBuilt to what you actually asked for, not a template with empty sections.","product"),
"78_app_progression": ("B2C","Your next target comes from your own numbers.\n\nNot a percentage of something you guessed on day one. You log week two, and week three sets targets from what you actually lifted.\n\nThat's progressive overload actually applied, rather than 'add 2.5kg and hope' 📈","strength"),
"79_app_no_login": ("B2C","No app store. No login. No password to forget.\n\nNothing to download, nothing to sign into. Save the link to your home screen and it opens like any other app.\n\nLost it? One page, your email, and we send it straight back.","product"),
"80_app_cycles": ("B2C","Run the same block twice and it keeps both.\n\nCycle one's numbers stay exactly where they are. Cycle two starts above them.\n\nThe first version of this quietly overwrote your old logs. Took me an embarrassingly long time to spot. It doesn't now 🙃","product"),
"81_app_holds": ("B2C","It times the hold, not just the rest.\n\nTwelve seconds. Not 'as long as possible'. Holding to failure trains failure. Holding to a target trains the position.\n\nStatic work needs a number to beat, same as anything else.","calisthenics"),
"82_app_swap": ("B2C","Rack taken? Now you can swap it sensibly.\n\nIf you know the point of the exercise, you know what can replace it. Loading the hamstring at length? A good morning, a single-leg version, or a machine curl all do that.\n\nA plan that explains itself survives contact with a busy gym.","strength"),
"83_app_week_view": ("B2C","Four weeks, and you can see all of them.\n\nLook ahead if you want to. Most people don't, and that's fine.\n\nWeek four backs off on purpose. That's where the adaptation actually lands. A block, not a list.","strength"),
"84_app_coach_branded": ("B2B","Coaches, it goes out looking like yours, not ours.\n\nYour programme, your notes attached to the exercises, your name on it. You wrote it, you reviewed it, you changed what you disagreed with.\n\nYour client just gets it somewhere they'll actually open.\n\nDM me for a look, five minutes, no pitch 👋","coaches"),
}
